    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can you provide a summary of the debate between originalism and living constitutionalism as it pertains specifically to the interpretation of the Second Amendment?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The debate between originalism and living constitutionalism centers on the interpretation of the Second Amendment. Originalists argue that the Second Amendment's text, given its historical context, should be taken literally, giving individuals a right to keep and bear arms for the original purposes of a militia. In contrast, living constitutionalists interpret the Second Amendment's meaning to evolve over time, considering its relevance to public safety and individual right to self-defense. This difference in perspective affects how the Supreme Court interprets and applies the Second Amendment's protected right. The disagreement has led to divided opinions on gun control laws and regulations in the US.",
