      "content": "That's a decent start, but it feels a bit surface-level. Could you go deeper into the legal reasoning for each? Specifically, I'm interested in the strongest scholarly arguments for both sides. I want to understand what makes the originalist framework so compelling to many jurists, but I also want a rigorous look at the legitimate legal theories used by living constitutionalists to justify a modern reading.",
